monitored in a subset of 54 patients. Sixteen neutral words were played 20 times during surgery and, on recovery, 
implicit memory for these words was tested with a word identification task. Explicit memory for the surgical period was 
tested with a structured interview. Behavioural changes were assessed with age-appropriate questionnaires.              
