fentanyl 5 micrograms/kg prior to sternotomy and fentanyl 10 micrograms/kg with midazolam 0.1 mg/kg at commencement of 
cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB). Patients receiving propofol were extubated earlier (median 9.1 h versus 12.3 h, P = 
0.006), although there was no difference in time to intensive care unit (ICU) discharge (both 22 h, P = 0.54). Both 
groups had similar hemodynamic changes throughout (all P > 0.10), as well as metaraminol (P = 0.49) and inotrope 
