│ Isoflurane and xenon at 0.8 MAC reduced the BIS to a median of 40 (range 36-53) and 36 (30-61), respectively. With   │
│ decreasing concentrations of isoflurane, the BIS increased progressively and it reached a median of 96 (90-98) when  │
│ the patients awoke. In contrast, four patients receiving xenon responded to verbal command while the BIS was below   │
│ 50 [median 45 (range 41-49)]. The remaining seven patients in the xenon group awoke when their BIS was greater than  │
│ 80 [median 96 (range 82-98)], but in four of them the BIS was no greater than 50 when the xenon concentration was    │
│ only 0.1 MAC (7%) higher than that associated with awakening. We conclude that low BIS values (< 50) do not          │
