│ deltoid muscle 15 min. before anaesthesia (GA) in patients elicited for laparoscopic cholecystectomy (LCHE). GA was  │
│ performed in a standard way, ECG, NIBP, respiration rate, SpO2, onset of effect, Observers Assessment of Alertness   │
│ Sedation Score (OAASS) before GA, circulatory reaction to intubation and capnoperitoneum, fentanyl consumption       │
│ during GA, time to the first request for post-operative analgesia and postoperative nausea and vomiting were         │
│ measured. The data were processed by Kruskal-Wallis and Fisher tests. P-value < 0.05 was considered significant.     │
│ RESULTS There were 16 patients in FNT and Dolsin and 15 patients in ALFNT with no differences in demography except   │
│ for younger age in ALFNT. The main differences were in hypertension during capnoperitoneum: 0/16 FNT and 1/15 ALFNT  │
│ vs. 11/16 Dolsin, both p < 0.001, per-operative fentanyl consumption: FNT 31.5 microg vs. Dolsin 165.0 microg, p <   │
│ 0.001 and ALFNT 50.0 microg, p < 0.05 (ALFNT vs. Dolsin, p < 0.01) and request to the first analgesic post surgery:  │
│ FNT 1.3 h. vs. Dolsin 0.45 h., p < 0.05 vs. ALFNT 0.8 h., p < 0.01. There were no differences in side effects except │
│ for bradycardia in ALFNT (p < 0.05). CONCLUSIONS Dexmedetomidine-ketamine-fentanyl-atropine combination is superior  │
│ to pethidine-atropine combination in suppressing of adverse hemodynamic effects of capnoperitoneum, decreased need   │
│ for analgesia during GA and prolonged postoperative analgesia."}, {"study_index": 397, "title": "Effects of the      │
